1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:11,290
Two clips, different sizes. Join with -c copy.

2
00:00:11,290 --> 00:00:19,310
Does FFmpeg stop you? Warn you?

3
00:00:19,310 --> 00:00:30,940
A: 320x180, 50 frames. B: 640x360, 50 frames.

4
00:00:30,940 --> 00:00:42,570
Docs: all files must have the same streams.

5
00:00:42,570 --> 00:00:50,260
Exit code 0. Zero warning lines.

6
00:00:50,260 --> 00:00:55,390
A file came out.

7
00:00:55,390 --> 00:01:04,260
Header: 320x180, 100 frames, 4 s.

8
00:01:04,260 --> 00:01:08,690
Nothing mentions 640x360.

9
00:01:08,690 --> 00:01:17,730
Inside: 50 at 320x180, 50 at 640x360.

10
00:01:17,730 --> 00:01:25,470
Decode problems: 0. Players: not tested.

11
00:01:25,470 --> 00:01:34,430
Same-size control: 100 frames, all 320x180.

12
00:01:34,430 --> 00:01:47,880
Re-encode with scale and pad: all 100 at 640x360.

13
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:56,060
Silent success is not proof.

14
00:01:56,060 --> 00:02:05,880
Not tested: players, editors, other codecs.
